The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (sbi->sync_decompress == EROFS_SYNC_DECOMPRESS_AUTO)
    sbi->sync_decompress = EROFS_SYNC_DECOMPRESS_FORCE_ON;
Reason:
These lines were placed after queuing decompression work (via `queue_work` or `kthread_queue_work`). This ordering creates a race condition: if the queued work completes quickly (unlocking all folios), the filesystem unmount can proceed and free the `sbi` structure before the assignment to `sbi->sync_decompress` executes, resulting in a use-after-free access.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (sbi->sync_decompress == EROFS_SYNC_DECOMPRESS_AUTO)
    sbi->sync_decompress = EROFS_SYNC_DECOMPRESS_FORCE_ON;
Reason:
These lines are moved to occur *before* any decompression work is queued. By updating `sbi->sync_decompress` prior to enqueuing work, the assignment is completed before the work can potentially lead to filesystem unmount, thus eliminating the use-after-free race condition.

